    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0197" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg191"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In accordance with a request made to me by
                    the governor-general of Canada, acting under instructions from Her Majesty’s
                    Government, I have the honor to transmit herewith, for the information of the
                    United States Government, a copy of a minute<anchor n="2" xml:id="d207-f1"/> of
                    his excellency’s council, dated the 16th ultimo, to which is appended a complete
                    list of such British vessels as have cleared from Canadian ports for the sealing
                    grounds during the present season.</p>
                <p>Of these vessels it appears that 34 have cleared for the coast of Japan and 24
                    for the American coast, making in all 48.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
